The audit reports how many characters and estimated tokens Hermes adds to each
profile's prompt. It must count the same text Hermes adds, but it does not import
Hermes itself, so these files carry verbatim copies of Hermes prompt text, taken
from agent/prompt_builder.py, agent/system_prompt.py and
tools/memory_tool_store.py in Hermes Agent:

- audit/vendor/profile_context.py: the default agent identity, the built-in
  guidance strings (help, task completion, parallel tool calls, tool-use
  enforcement, model-specific execution guidance, skills, session search,
  mid-turn steering), the memory guidance, the skills index header and
  footer, and related constants.
- audit/skill_packs.py: the skills index header and footer and the note for a
  skill that cannot be loaded.
- audit/facts.py: the marker Hermes inserts when it truncates a context file.

The copies exist so the audit can rebuild and measure that text.

